{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2907","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2907","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2907\",\"parent_revision\":\"c3c84397dcf7ac5b0eb6d0863c82b5aef9a8e3503cedd29dd4e78e9353a2feb7\",\"root_revision\":\"c3c84397dcf7ac5b0eb6d0863c82b5aef9a8e3503cedd29dd4e78e9353a2feb7\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDiscovered while fixing #2899 (PR #2906). GitHubBackend.put_content() (artifact manifests, artifact content, plans, dispatch plans) attempts a direct GitHub Contents API commit to main. This repo's branch-protection ruleset (required_status_checks) rejects direct commits to main, so every such write exhausts its retries and falls back to a durably-queued local pending mutation in ~/.dh/projects/.../github-cache. PR #2906 fixed the read side so a caller sharing that same local cache sees its own pending write correctly (read-your-own-writes), but the underlying commit itself never succeeds \u2014 content stays queued-and-retrying forever and is invisible to any other machine, worktree, or CI run that doesn't share that exact local cache file. Needs a design decision: should these writes go through a PR instead of a direct branch commit, or should the ruleset carve out an exception for this bot/token, or should content storage move off direct-to-main commits entirely (e.g. a dedicated non-protected branch/ref)?\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Not specified\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-16\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **refactor(backlog-mcp): artifact/plan content writes never land \u2014 github ruleset blocks direct contents api commits to main** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b6cbc564a8aad3955ed3607103cc1e33c6676e0cc0eb0267aff4ed45c1dc6aa6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS67OQ\"}"}